WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.920
Texture records cooling history. Slow cooling gives crystals time to grow

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:09.489
large. Faster cooling makes small crystals; very rapid cooling can make

00:00:09.489 --> 00:00:09.905
glass.

00:00:10.725 --> 00:00:15.451
Watch the two-stage sample. Large crystals grow first during slow cooling.

00:00:15.451 --> 00:00:20.178
Faster cooling then produces the fine groundmass. That mixed texture is

00:00:20.178 --> 00:00:20.607
porphyritic.

00:00:21.433 --> 00:00:26.185
Explain the history, not just the texture name. He also emphasized

00:00:26.185 --> 00:00:30.936
pegmatites: water-rich melt helps atoms move efficiently and grow exceptionally large

00:00:30.936 --> 00:00:31.368
crystals.
